From 389937e86e3db3001bcfcef8c014b2efe4475112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:00:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] campaign: full RoC+TFT campaign playable in the browser

Campaign flow lands end to end: the campaign select lists all nine
campaigns (five Reign of Chaos, four Frozen Throne) with backdrops, the
mission list shows chapters plus the authored intro/open/end cinematics
(camera rows; the browser build plays them through the page overlay since
it no longer gates them behind BZ_FFMPEG), and missions launch through the
normal map loader.

- single_player.c: cinematic rows also in __EMSCRIPTEN__ builds;
  model-cinematic finale rows (Doodads\Cinematic\...\*.mdl) route to
  the movie import instead of the map loader.
- cl_movie.c: CL_PlayMovie passes .mdl/.mdx paths to CL_PlayModelCinematic
  (engine-rendered ending scene) on every platform.
- common.c: FS_ResolveMapPath fetches a missing explicit map before the
  existence probe, so campaign paths like Campaign/Classic/ROC/*.w3m
  resolve on demand from the served mirror.
- campaign_progress.c: browser builds mirror the progress file through
  localStorage so a reload resumes the campaign.
- api natives: 80+ names the campaign scripts and Blizzard.j call now
  exist (destructable skin creators, IsUnitIdType, AoE damage, dialogue
  keys, item flags, multiboard getters, ability/unit field setters as
  accepted no-ops with follow-up notes).  Missing natives unwind whole
  triggers, so a complete set is what lets missions run.
- tools: gen-campaign-strings.py builds literal CampaignStrings[_exp].txt
  from the Reforged campaigninfo + enUS globalstrings (124/124 keys).
